{"formula": "=AND(COUNTIF($B$2:B2,MAX($B$2:$B$7))=1,B2=MAX($B$2:$B$7))"}

The weekly scores in row 8 sit in columns E onward, so FR8 should average one month's weekly block. Row 5 holds each month's starting column number (FR5 is `=COLUMN(N8)`, and FS5 adds each month's week count). The formula follows the pattern in FR12:FR13: it builds the range from FR5 up to one column before FS5 and returns blank if the first week is empty.

I made the row-5 references absolute (`FR$5`, `FS$5`). The context doesn't show whether FR12 and FR13 use `$`, so that is my assumption to keep the column lookup correct.

{"formula": "=IF(INDIRECT(ADDRESS(ROW(FP8),FR$5))=\"\",\"\",AVERAGE(INDIRECT(ADDRESS(ROW(FP8),FR$5) & \":\" & ADDRESS(ROW(FP8),FS$5-1))))"}

